id: pm-39cqqx
title: Immutable-tree DeepScan and CodeFactor zero-new-issues release gate
description: "Make hosted static analysis a hard, locally executable release criterion across reviewed heads, merge commits, and squash commits. Prefer exact-commit results; permit reviewed-source evidence only when immutable Git trees match and squash association is unique, merged, and targets main. Fail closed on missing, pending, stale, skipped, malformed, ambiguous, or different-tree evidence."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:ci","area:quality",codefactor,deepscan,release-gate,static-analysis
created_at: "2026-07-24T22:46:08.676Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T01:25:57.539Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T00:56:51.324Z"
author: claude-code-agent
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "A local command fails for analyzer findings, absent or pending checks, malformed payloads, ambiguous squash associations, unavailable tree provenance, and non-identical trees; It passes exact reviewed heads and identical-tree GitHub merge or squash commits while reporting the analyzed SHA and bounded provenance source; Strict release readiness invokes the command and main branch protection requires both analyzers; Focused tests, lint, typecheck, full literal 100/100/100/100 coverage, hosted checks, and live merged-squash verification pass"
parent: pm-92if
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "Release readiness fails closed unless the release tree has immutable reviewed evidence proving DeepScan zero new issues, CodeFactor no issues, and strict protected-main requirements for both contexts."
actual_result: The release gate remains exact-commit-first and now accepts reviewed merge-parent or squash-PR evidence only after immutable tree equality. Squash fallback additionally requires one GitHub-associated closed PR merged into main with the release commit as merge_commit_sha. Ten fail-closed provenance cases and live main acceptance pass; full repository coverage remains literal 100/100/100/100.
